Subject: Read two arguments into registers with one instruction

What this does
  Adds the register opcode `get_arg2`, which copies two argument slots into
  two registers. The post-allocation fusion pairs adjacent `get_arg`
  instructions when no branch target or block start other than their shared
  entry falls between them, which halves the prologue that loads a
  function's promoted arguments into their home registers. The loader's slot
  check bounds both argument operands.

Why we need it
  Every function starts with one `get_arg` dispatch per promoted parameter;
  `get_arg` is 11.5% of Octane earleyboyer's dispatches, 8.2% of raytrace's
  and 7.7% of splay's, and `get_arg -> get_arg` is the most frequent pair in
  earleyboyer and raytrace.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  Yes, it adds a register opcode; 9999-bc-version-bump covers it.

Notes
  Copying the arguments while the call builds the frame would remove the
  prologue entirely, but every entry path (light, record, generator and the
  monolith) would have to perform the copy; pairing keeps the program
  self-contained.


